.TH RC 1 "August 2026" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rc \- rune compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rc
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file.rn ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rc
is a lightweight compiler for the Rune programming language,
targeting x86\-i386.
It compiles
.B .rn
source files into x86 AT&T assembly (a
.B .s
file), and by default also assembles and links them into a native
binary through
.BR cc .
.PP
Rune resembles assembly but with variables, pointers, and loops.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-compile, \-c
Compile and assemble only, do not link.
Produces a
.B .o
file per input.
.TP
.B \-debug, \-d
Print extra info about the compiling process.
.TP
.B \-help, \-h
Print usage information.
.TP
.B \-out, \-o FILE
Set the output name (default
.BR a.out ).
.TP
.B \-S
Compile only, emit assembly (a
.B .s
file) and stop.
.TP
.B \-Verbose, \-V
Enables log output.
.TP
.B \-version, \-v
Show version and copyright.
.SH OUTPUT
By default every input
.B file.rn
is compiled, assembled, and linked into
.BR a.out ;
the intermediate
.B .s
and
.B .o
files are removed.
With
.B \-c
the process stops after assembling, leaving
.BR file.o ,
and with
.B \-S
it stops after compiling, leaving
.BR file.s .
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile, assemble, link, and run:
.RS
.nf
$ rc file.rn
$ ./a.out
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop at an intermediate stage or rename the output:
.RS
.nf
$ rc \-S file.rn # emits file.s
$ rc \-c file.rn # emits file.o
$ rc \-o prog file.rn # outputs ./prog
.fi
.RE
